            <ArticleTitle>Multiple coronary cameral fistulae: a rare anomaly and cause of ischaemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e1-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5830/CVJA-2010-097</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 82-year-old hypertensive, diabetic woman was admitted to our department for pre-operative cardiac evaluation. A myocardial perfusion scan revealed apicoseptal and inferior segment hypoperfusion. Coronary angiography exhibited extensive multiple coronary cameral fistulae draining into the left ventricle in a homogeneous and circular way.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
